IMPORT prelude

-- Terrorism (Suppression of Misuse of Radioactive Material) Act 2017 (Singapore) -- what counts as nuclear and radioactive material
-- (s 2), the activities the Act does not reach (s 3), the offences of possessing, making and using radioactive material or a
-- "Convention device", using or damaging a nuclear facility, threats, demands and attempts (ss 4 to 10) and their punishments, what
-- a "nuclear terrorism offence" is and its reach outside Singapore (ss 2, 11), the political-offence exception (ss 12(1), 13(7)(c)),
-- and the Public Prosecutor's consent (s 14).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation ("version in force from 1/7/2022"), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/TSMRMA2017.txt. The revised edition "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021";
-- the latest amendment annotated is Act 17 of 2022 wef 01/07/2022 (to s 13, extradition).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0122 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: Tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a
-- sharper question yet. For an ordinary person or business the answer is: which conduct with radioactive material is a crime, what
-- the defences built into the offences are ("without lawful authority", the intent elements), and how heavily each is punished.
-- Not encoded: the detail of extradition under s 13(2) to (6) (Gazette notifications, declared Commonwealth territories, treaties),
-- the definitions of "criminal matter" and "relevant offence" beyond their effect, the definitions of "conveyance", "government",
-- "ionising radiation" and "military forces of a State" beyond the s 3 flags, and the Penal Code provisions the Act refers to
-- (ss 34, 35 and 300(a)) -- their content is not in the deposit.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions of the example rows. No pipeline, no coverage
-- table, no independent test pass, no human gate. NOT for public use. See NOTES.md.

§ `Terrorism (Suppression of Misuse of Radioactive Material) Act 2017`

§§ `2 -- nuclear material and radioactive material`

-- s 2 "nuclear material" means (a) "plutonium, except plutonium with an isotopic concentration of plutonium-238 exceeding 80%";
-- (b) "uranium-233"; (c) uranium in which the abundance ratio of uranium-233 and uranium-235 to uranium-238 "is greater than the
-- ratio of uranium-235 to uranium-238 occurring in nature"; (d) "uranium with an isotopic concentration equal to that occurring in
-- nature, but not in the form of ore or ore residue"; or (e) "any material containing one or more of the materials mentioned in
-- paragraphs (a) to (d)".
-- The natural ratio is not stated in the Act, so uranium is classified by kind, not by number.
DECLARE Material IS ONE OF
    `plutonium`
    `uranium-233`
    `enriched uranium`
    `refined natural uranium`
    `natural uranium ore or ore residue`
    `depleted uranium`
    `a material containing nuclear material`
    `another radioactive substance`

GIVEN `the material` IS A Material, `percentage of plutonium-238` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the material is nuclear material` IF
    CONSIDER `the material`
    WHEN `plutonium` THEN `percentage of plutonium-238` <= 80
    WHEN `uranium-233` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `enriched uranium` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `refined natural uranium` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a material containing nuclear material` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 2 "radioactive material" means "any nuclear material or any other radioactive substance".
-- "radioactive substance" means any substance (a) that contains nuclides "that undergo spontaneous disintegration accompanied by the
-- emission of one or more types of ionising radiation"; AND (b) that, "owing to its radiological or fissile properties, may cause"
-- death or serious bodily injury, or substantial damage to property or the environment.
-- Nuclear material is radioactive material without any harm test; anything else must pass both limbs.
GIVEN `the material` IS A Material, `percentage of plutonium-238` IS A NUMBER,
      `it emits ionising radiation by spontaneous disintegration` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `its radiological or fissile properties may cause death, serious injury or substantial damage` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the material is radioactive material` IF
        `the material is nuclear material` `the material` `percentage of plutonium-238`
    OR  (    `it emits ionising radiation by spontaneous disintegration`
         AND `its radiological or fissile properties may cause death, serious injury or substantial damage`)

§§ `3 -- activities the Act does not apply to`

-- s 3: the Act does not apply to "(a) the activities of armed forces during an armed conflict, as those terms are understood under
-- international humanitarian law, which are governed by that law"; "(b) the activities undertaken by military forces of a State in
-- the exercise of their official duties, to the extent that those activities are governed by other rules of international law".
-- s 2: "armed conflict" "does not include internal disturbances and tensions, such as riots".
GIVEN `armed forces acting in an armed conflict governed by international humanitarian law` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `military forces on official duties governed by other rules of international law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act applies` IF
        (NOT `armed forces acting in an armed conflict governed by international humanitarian law`)
    AND (NOT `military forces on official duties governed by other rules of international law`)

§§ `4 to 7 -- possessing, making and using`

-- s 4: guilty if the person, "intentionally and without lawful authority, possesses any radioactive material or Convention device";
-- and intends it "be used to cause" death or serious bodily injury, or substantial damage to property or the environment.
-- s 5: the same for one who "makes any Convention device".
-- s 6(1): the same for one who "uses in any way" radioactive material or a Convention device, with a third intent: "(iii) to compel
-- any other person, or any international organisation or government, to do or refrain from doing any act".
-- s 7(1): one who "uses or damages a nuclear facility in a manner that causes, or creates a risk of, the release of radioactive
-- material", with the same three intents as s 6.
-- The intent to compel completes ss 6 and 7 but not ss 4 and 5.
DECLARE Conduct IS ONE OF
    `possessing radioactive material or a Convention device`
    `making a Convention device`
    `using radioactive material or a Convention device`
    `using or damaging a nuclear facility`

GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct,
      `done intentionally` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `with lawful authority` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `intends death or serious bodily injury` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `intends substantial damage to property or the environment` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `intends to compel a person, organisation or government` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `causes or risks a release of radioactive material` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the conduct is an offence` IF
        `done intentionally`
    AND (NOT `with lawful authority`)
    AND CONSIDER `the conduct`
        WHEN `possessing radioactive material or a Convention device` THEN
                `intends death or serious bodily injury` OR `intends substantial damage to property or the environment`
        WHEN `making a Convention device` THEN
                `intends death or serious bodily injury` OR `intends substantial damage to property or the environment`
        WHEN `using radioactive material or a Convention device` THEN
                `intends death or serious bodily injury` OR `intends substantial damage to property or the environment`
                OR `intends to compel a person, organisation or government`
        WHEN `using or damaging a nuclear facility` THEN
                `causes or risks a release of radioactive material`
            AND (   `intends death or serious bodily injury` OR `intends substantial damage to property or the environment`
                 OR `intends to compel a person, organisation or government`)

§§ `8 to 10 -- threats, demands and attempts`

-- s 8: "Any person who threatens to do any act that would be an offence under section 6 or 7 shall be guilty of an offence".
-- A threat to possess or make (ss 4, 5) is not within s 8.
GIVEN `the threatened conduct` IS A Conduct, `the threatened act would meet every element of that offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the threat is an offence` IF
        `the threatened act would meet every element of that offence`
    AND CONSIDER `the threatened conduct`
        WHEN `using radioactive material or a Convention device` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `using or damaging a nuclear facility` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 9: guilty if the offender, "intentionally and without lawful authority, demands that another person" (i) make available, or
-- (ii) give access to, "any radioactive material, Convention device or nuclear facility"; "and (b) the demand is made or accompanied
-- by the use of force or by threats of any kind".
GIVEN `demanded intentionally` IS A BOOLEAN, `demanded with lawful authority` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `demanded material, a device or a facility be made available or access given` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the demand used force or threats` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the demand is an offence` IF
        `demanded intentionally`
    AND (NOT `demanded with lawful authority`)
    AND `demanded material, a device or a facility be made available or access given`
    AND `the demand used force or threats`

-- s 10: "Any person who attempts to commit an offence under section 4, 5, 6 or 7, or attempts to cause such an offence to be
-- committed, and in such attempt does any act towards the commission of the offence".
GIVEN `attempted an offence under ss 4 to 7` IS A BOOLEAN, `did an act towards its commission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the attempt is an offence` IF
    `attempted an offence under ss 4 to 7` AND `did an act towards its commission`

§§ `4 to 10 -- punishment`

-- ss 4, 5: "liable on conviction to imprisonment for a term which may extend to life imprisonment".
-- ss 6(2), 7(2): "(a) in any case where the person intends the use ... to cause the death of any individual, and death is caused --
-- be subject to the same punishment as an act under section 300(a) of the Penal Code 1871; or (b) in any other case -- be punished
-- with imprisonment for life". The deposit does not say what the s 300(a) punishment is.
-- s 8 (threat) and s 9 (demand): "not exceeding 10 years". s 10 (attempt): "not exceeding 15 years".
-- Under s 6(2)(a) only an intent to cause DEATH, with death caused, attracts the s 300(a) punishment; an intent to injure that ends in
-- a death is "any other case": life imprisonment.
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `the s 4 possession offence`
    `the s 5 making offence`
    `the s 6 use offence`
    `the s 7 nuclear facility offence`
    `the s 8 threat offence`
    `the s 9 demand offence`
    `the s 10 attempt offence`

DECLARE Punishment IS ONE OF
    `imprisonment which may extend to life`
    `imprisonment for life`
    `the same punishment as Penal Code s 300(a)`
    `imprisonment up to 15 years`
    `imprisonment up to 10 years`

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence, `intended to cause death` IS A BOOLEAN, `death was caused` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Punishment
DECIDE `the punishment` IS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `the s 4 possession offence` THEN `imprisonment which may extend to life`
    WHEN `the s 5 making offence` THEN `imprisonment which may extend to life`
    WHEN `the s 6 use offence` THEN
        IF `intended to cause death` AND `death was caused` THEN `the same punishment as Penal Code s 300(a)` ELSE `imprisonment for life`
    WHEN `the s 7 nuclear facility offence` THEN
        IF `intended to cause death` AND `death was caused` THEN `the same punishment as Penal Code s 300(a)` ELSE `imprisonment for life`
    WHEN `the s 8 threat offence` THEN `imprisonment up to 10 years`
    WHEN `the s 9 demand offence` THEN `imprisonment up to 10 years`
    WHEN `the s 10 attempt offence` THEN `imprisonment up to 15 years`

-- ss 4 and 5 say "liable ... may extend to"; ss 6(2)(b) and 7(2)(b) say "shall ... be punished with imprisonment for life".
GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence, `intended to cause death` IS A BOOLEAN, `death was caused` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court must impose life imprisonment` IF
    `the punishment` `the offence` `intended to cause death` `death was caused` EQUALS `imprisonment for life`

§§ `2 and 11 -- nuclear terrorism offences and their reach`

-- s 2 "nuclear terrorism offence" means "(a) an offence under section 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9 or 10; (b) an abetment of or a conspiracy to
-- commit an offence under section 4, 5, 6, 7, 8 or 9; or (c)" joint liability under Penal Code ss 34 or 35.
-- Paragraph (b) omits s 10: abetting or conspiring to commit an ATTEMPT is not listed.
DECLARE Involvement IS ONE OF
    `committing it`
    `abetting it`
    `conspiring to commit it`

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence, `the involvement` IS A Involvement
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is a nuclear terrorism offence` IF
    CONSIDER `the involvement`
    WHEN `committing it` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE
        CONSIDER `the offence`
        WHEN `the s 10 attempt offence` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 11: "Any person who, outside Singapore, commits an act that, if committed in Singapore, would constitute a nuclear terrorism
-- offence is deemed to commit the act in Singapore and may be proceeded against, charged, tried and punished accordingly."
-- Nationality and the place of the act do not matter.
GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence, `the involvement` IS A Involvement, `done outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it may be tried in Singapore` IF
    `it is a nuclear terrorism offence` `the offence` `the involvement`

§§ `12(1) and 13 -- political-offence exception and extradition`

-- s 12(1): for mutual assistance under Part 3 of the Mutual Assistance in Criminal Matters Act 2000 "to a Convention country for a
-- criminal matter involving a relevant offence of that country, the relevant offence is deemed not to be an offence of a political
-- character". s 13(1): "Every nuclear terrorism offence is deemed to be an extradition offence" for Parts 3, 4 and 5 of the
-- Extradition Act 1968; s 13(7)(c): any such offence "is deemed not to be an offence of a political character".
-- A "Convention country" is "a foreign country that is a Party to the Convention".
GIVEN `the requesting country is a Party to the Convention` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the conduct would be a nuclear terrorism offence in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the political-offence objection is unavailable` IF
    `the requesting country is a Party to the Convention` AND `the conduct would be a nuclear terrorism offence in Singapore`

§§ `14 -- Public Prosecutor's consent`

-- s 14: "A prosecution under this Act must not be instituted except by or with the consent of the Public Prosecutor."
GIVEN `instituted by the Public Prosecutor` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Public Prosecutor consented` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the prosecution may be instituted` IF
    `instituted by the Public Prosecutor` OR `the Public Prosecutor consented`
